<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dae Joyeong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 719</span> · Also known as King Go of Balhae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dae Joyeong was the founder of Balhae, a kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. A former Goguryeo general, he led Goguryeo refugees and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohe">Mohe</a> tribesmen out of Tang control, defeated a Tang army at Tianmenling in 698 and founded his state at Mount Dongmou in Manchuria. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a> recognised him as king in 713.</p></div>
